course: dictionary
lesson: 8357
title: Words that turn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rotate is a verb. It means to turn around a centre or a point, like a spinning top. Its forms are rotate, rotates, rotated and rotating. When you see a word like «rotating», ask yourself: what is turning, and what is it turning around?
explain: Rotate can have more than one meaning. In maths it means turning a shape around a fixed point, and the shape keeps its size. In sport it can mean taking turns in a regular order. «Ella's coach in Bath has 10 players for 7 places and rotates them» means the coach changes who plays, in turn.
explain: Use the words around rotate to choose the right meaning. Drums, wheels and shapes all tell you that something is turning. Then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If "turns around a centre" still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Rotate means to turn around a centre or a point, or to spin.
fact: «Rotating» is the form of rotate used for something that is turning.
fact: In maths, to rotate a shape means to turn it around a fixed point by a certain angle, such as 90 degrees.
fact: «A tunnel-boring machine grinds through rock with a giant rotating cutting wheel.» Here rotating means spinning round.
fact: Rotate can also mean to take turns or change places in a regular order.
exercise: What does it mean to rotate a shape in maths? | To cut it into pieces | To make it bigger | *To turn it around a fixed point | To colour it in
exercise: «The Earth rotates once a day.» What is the Earth doing? | It is getting smaller | It is moving to a new sun | It is going dark for ever | *It is spinning around
exercise: «The sweets tumble in big rotating drums.» Find and copy the one word that shows the drums are turning. | *rotating | coat | big | sprayed
test: «Ella's coach in Bath rotates the players.» What does rotates mean here? | They turn into birds | *They take turns in a regular order | They spin on the pitch | They go home early
test: Which is true about a shape that has been rotated? | It changes size | It gets heavier | It loses its corners | *It keeps its size
exam: Lee says rotate means to shout loudly. Why is he wrong? | Rotate means to shout loudly, so he is right | Rotate means to sleep | *Rotate means to turn around a centre or a point | Rotate means to swim
